[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5196031422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122138#issuecomment-5196031422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122138","id":5196031422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNbUlvg","user":{"login":"MatthiasBae","id":52577744,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTc3NzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52577744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae","html_url":"https://github.com/MatthiasBae","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T18:55:17Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T18:55:17Z","body":"Your ToolExport Class needs to be a tool script too","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5196031422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5196983283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122138#issuecomment-5196983283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122138","id":5196983283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNcOr8w","user":{"login":"celestino","id":1292254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTIyNTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1292254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino","html_url":"https://github.com/celestino","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T20:29:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T20:49:17Z","body":"Thanks, @MatthiasBae! \nDoes this mean that every custom node referenced by a [Tool] script also has to be marked as [Tool], recursively?\n\nThat is exactly what I observed during testing.\n\nThe problem I see is that this requirement propagates through the entire composition hierarchy.\n\nFor example:\n```\nZ [Tool]\n└── references A\n    └── references B\n        └── references C\n            └── references D\n```\n\nIf Z is only using A, it seems that A, B, C, and D must all also be marked as [Tool], even though they don't contain any editor logic themselves.\n\nThis doesn't seem like the intended design, because:\n\n1. It forces implementation details (editor behavior) onto unrelated classes.\n2. It makes composition harder, since adding a single [Tool] script can require modifying an entire dependency chain.\n3. It potentially increases editor overhead by executing scripts that are only needed at runtime.\n\nInterestingly, this requirement does not apply to built-in Godot Control nodes, only to custom C# node types.\n\nIs this expected behavior, or is it a limitation/bug of the current C# [Tool] implementation?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5196983283/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5197530663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122138#issuecomment-5197530663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122138","id":5197530663,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNcwGJw","user":{"login":"celestino","id":1292254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTIyNTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1292254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino","html_url":"https://github.com/celestino","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celestino/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T21:25:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T21:32:27Z","body":"The main issue is not only that [Tool] propagates recursively.\n\nIt also forces runtime-only classes to execute in the editor.\n\nFor example, my custom Controll (InputIcon ) subscribes to runtime services in _Ready():\n\n```\nInputProvider.Get().InputChanged += OnInputChanged;\n```\n\nThese services are not available in the editor (which produce an error), so marking InputIcon as [Tool] forces me to add editor-specific guards (Engine.IsEditorHint()) to classes that otherwise contain no editor functionality.\n\nThis couples reusable runtime components to the editor solely because they are referenced by a [Tool] script.\n\n(Edit: Reduced the scope)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5197530663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5204532615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122138#issuecomment-5204532615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122138","id":5204532615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNjbdhw","user":{"login":"MatthiasBae","id":52577744,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTc3NzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52577744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae","html_url":"https://github.com/MatthiasBae","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T12:18:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T12:18:32Z","body":"> Does this mean that every custom node referenced by a [Tool] script also has to be marked as [Tool], recursively?\n\nYes and I think I have read somewhere that this is intended behaviour.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5204532615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5257007627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122138#issuecomment-5257007627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122138","id":5257007627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOVeSCw","user":{"login":"paulloz","id":437025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzAyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/437025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz","html_url":"https://github.com/paulloz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-11T18:07:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T19:03:44Z","body":"Thank you for reporting, this is already tracked in #119603, please see there for more details.\n\nI think if anything, this needs better documentation.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5257007627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]